Notebook[{
Cell["InfraPoint", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"c64f667d-b2ec-48a8-96a4-cd8b8acb804a"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"9272daf1-e99a-4d57-990e-d2cbe029b38f"],

Cell["\<\
InfraPoint[{v1, ..., vk}] is the unweighted multi-realisation form (each \
vertex mass 1); InfraPoint[{v1, ...}, {w1, ...}] carries explicit per-vertex \
mass. The canonical form has a duplicate-free support with positive masses \
that add on aggregation; an all-ones weighted form collapses to the bare \
1-arg form. Accessors [\"Support\"], [\"Weights\"], [\"Mass\"], [\"First\"]. \
Find* finders return a List of unary InfraPoint[{v}] wrappers; wrap with \
InfraPoint @ ... to collapse via auto-flatten (masses add). Scene-language \
variants InfraPoint[] / InfraPoint[\"Center\"] / InfraPoint[\"Periphery\"] / \
InfraPoint[origin, dist] / InfraPoint[n] are constructors used inside \
InfraScene. In InfraSceneHighlight a weighted InfraPoint renders as a mass \
heat-map (heaviest vertex brightest).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bbebb75-f9a0-4318-b05e-b6ae00da3c66"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"06af31ae-dbac-4017-9cc1-717173ebe9bb"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"996246aa-4254-4ea4-9f3c-d2854c6f6993"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"6c49a3a7-e939-4f49-8169-0775fe570a06"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b54cafb1-18b0-478e-ab71-f5db4ca3c9ef"],

Cell["EuclideanGeometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f6ad075e-2002-488b-8e2a-8fab970fa500"],

Cell["SyntheticInfrageometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c386f6ce-b441-48e5-963e-8a662620eadb"]
},
